(2497337, 343243, 22970, '<td valign="top">I dont get the since of any empty room in your shot.</td>', 'I dont get the since of any empty room in your shot.', '2006-06-08 01:11:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2497386, 343176, 22970, '<td valign="top">Ok keep it real here. The photo is not bad but I have a few issues with it. The main one is the horizontal line that bends and goes down to the child''s head. That is very distracting. It also, with the bend, ends up almost in the center of the picture make the picture look like it is split. I think, in this photo, black and white or some other duotone would of worked better than the colored version. Everything from the child, floor, walls, and doors seem to have the yellowish tint. And the border does not do anything to help that. I think maybe positioning the child near the glass pane door with a reflection or shadow coming it would of helped. With that said you did meet the challenge.</td>', 'Ok keep it real here. The photo is not bad but I have a few issues with it. The main one is the horizontal line that bends and goes down to the child''s head. That is very distracting. It also, with the bend, ends up almost in the center of the picture make the picture look like it is split. I think, in this photo, black and white or some other duotone would of worked better than the colored version. Everything from the child, floor, walls, and doors seem to have the yellowish tint. And the border does not do anything to help that. I think maybe positioning the child near the glass pane door with a reflection or shadow coming it would of helped. With that said you did meet the challenge.', '2006-06-08 01:22:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2497405, 343212, 40642, '<td valign="top">So sweeeet!Love the black &amp; white and it being off-centered.</td>', 'So sweeeet!Love the black & white and it being off-centered.', '2006-06-08 01:29:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2497456, 343231, 22970, '<td valign="top">Good photo but I do have a few issues with it that I think you could of solved and it would of been better. First I will start with what hits me the most, your vertical highlight/reflection lines. They are splitting the photograph up. Example: the line on the right side of the brass fireplace front reflect on the hardwood floor goes all the way through the photograph making it looks like the right side of the photo is on another page. Also there are spots on the nice polished wood floor that in advanced editing could of been cloned out making for a nice smooth finish. I feel your crop is to tight to associate the picture with the challenge. I feel I am standing between to sofa''s. I think the picture would of given me a since of empty room if the picture were further away with an wider angle or maybe even of to the side at an angle. Remember I was telling you about the lines splitting up the photo? well the placement of your object (in the middle of the frame) only enhances the splitting feel. I think it would of looked better on the left side. With dodge and burn being an option in this challenge I think I would of burned the left lower portion of the photograph to make it like the right lower side and continue along the bottom so that it would of cut off the reflection lines keeping the photo together.<br/> <br/>With all that said you have good focus and lighting and your subject to create interest. Very nice wood finish, both walls and floor. I wish you well in the challenge.<br/>SDW</td>', 'Good photo but I do have a few issues with it that I think you could of solved and it would of been better. First I will start with what hits me the most, your vertical highlight/reflection lines. They are splitting the photograph up. Example: the line on the right side of the brass fireplace front reflect on the hardwood floor goes all the way through the photograph making it looks like the right side of the photo is on another page. Also there are spots on the nice polished wood floor that in advanced editing could of been cloned out making for a nice smooth finish. I feel your crop is to tight to associate the picture with the challenge. I feel I am standing between to sofa''s. I think the picture would of given me a since of empty room if the picture were further away with an wider angle or maybe even of to the side at an angle. Remember I was telling you about the lines splitting up the photo? well the placement of your object (in the middle of the frame) only enhances the splitting feel. I think it would of looked better on the left side. With dodge and burn being an option in this challenge I think I would of burned the left lower portion of the photograph to make it like the right lower side and continue along the bottom so that it would of cut off the reflection lines keeping the photo together. With all that said you have good focus and lighting and your subject to create interest. Very nice wood finish, both walls and floor. I wish you well in the challenge.SDW', '2006-06-08 01:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
