(2508133, 342312, 30861, '<td valign="top">*** C R I T I Q U E  C L U B  C O M M E N T ***<br/> <br/>There''s really nothing much to say about this except congrats on a personal best and a top-20 shot.<br/> <br/>You clearly shot in available light, so no critique of the lighting is relevant. It''s a little flat, but it is what it is. The color looks perhaps a little muddy, but it works very well. The composition is straightforward and interesting. It''s perhaps not as sharp as it might be (a little more USM in processing?) but it''s pretty good for an S9000.<br/> <br/>What really works about this picture is the subject itself; it''s a wonderful puzzle trying to figure out what the heck this "room" IS... Hopefully, you''ll post in your notes and tell us :-)<br/> <br/>Good work!<br/> <br/>Robt.</td>', '*** C R I T I Q U E  C L U B  C O M M E N T *** There''s really nothing much to say about this except congrats on a personal best and a top-20 shot. You clearly shot in available light, so no critique of the lighting is relevant. It''s a little flat, but it is what it is. The color looks perhaps a little muddy, but it works very well. The composition is straightforward and interesting. It''s perhaps not as sharp as it might be (a little more USM in processing?) but it''s pretty good for an S9000. What really works about this picture is the subject itself; it''s a wonderful puzzle trying to figure out what the heck this "room" IS... Hopefully, you''ll post in your notes and tell us :-) Good work! Robt.', '2006-06-12 01:47:14.000000', NULL, 0),
