(2510590, 343047, 53964, '<td valign="top">Rikki, I love this image. It brings back wonderful memories of the time I''ve spent in the Rockies, and it also makes me wonder just what you''re thinking as you sit there.<br/>The only nitpick I have at all is that the bright blue in the mtns distracts me a bit. Personally, I would mute that just a touch. <br/>I really don''t understand the low score!</td>', 'Rikki, I love this image. It brings back wonderful memories of the time I''ve spent in the Rockies, and it also makes me wonder just what you''re thinking as you sit there.The only nitpick I have at all is that the bright blue in the mtns distracts me a bit. Personally, I would mute that just a touch. I really don''t understand the low score!', '2006-06-12 21:26:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2510623, 343047, 6519, '<td valign="top">Since you asked in a thread......<br/>I dare to differ from the general after-challenge praise, sorry.<br/>I didn''t score it, but would have given it a 5 or a 6, and here is why:<br/> <br/>The b+w inside jumped out at me as having been desaturated. It''s not in keeping with the true nature of the place. By looking so unnatural and "wrong", it holds my attention and achieves the exact opposite of what you were trying to achieve (as per your notes). I would have preferred to see it left the natural color, but perhaps darkened a little if that was necessary.<br/> <br/>Much of the sky is blown and the colors outside look over saturated to me.<br/> <br/>This whole photo is really all about the view, not the empty room. It fits the challenge, but only in a happenstance way.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Since you asked in a thread......I dare to differ from the general after-challenge praise, sorry.I didn''t score it, but would have given it a 5 or a 6, and here is why: The b+w inside jumped out at me as having been desaturated. It''s not in keeping with the true nature of the place. By looking so unnatural and "wrong", it holds my attention and achieves the exact opposite of what you were trying to achieve (as per your notes). I would have preferred to see it left the natural color, but perhaps darkened a little if that was necessary. Much of the sky is blown and the colors outside look over saturated to me. This whole photo is really all about the view, not the empty room. It fits the challenge, but only in a happenstance way. ', '2006-06-12 21:40:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2510832, 343151, 53572, '<td valign="top">this was shot with a lensbaby.  no post processing blurring at all - in fact i sharpened with high pass!  looking back i probably should have used a smaller aperture (a little rubber/metal ring that you slip on top of the optic in a lensbaby!), but i was carried away with the whole newness of the lensbaby, baby!  it''s a very steep learning curve with this lens.  i shot about 30 of this, to get the focus i wanted.  i ended up having to sit in the hallway just to get this much of the room in the view. i was probably about 25 feet away from the trunk.</td>', 'this was shot with a lensbaby.  no post processing blurring at all - in fact i sharpened with high pass!  looking back i probably should have used a smaller aperture (a little rubber/metal ring that you slip on top of the optic in a lensbaby!), but i was carried away with the whole newness of the lensbaby, baby!  it''s a very steep learning curve with this lens.  i shot about 30 of this, to get the focus i wanted.  i ended up having to sit in the hallway just to get this much of the room in the view. i was probably about 25 feet away from the trunk.', '2006-06-12 23:06:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2510901, 343047, 8367, '<td valign="top">I would have given this a 5. The colors are too oversaturated and the blacks are "clogged". No more laptop for you! :)<br/>It''s hard to do a sp. Getting the focus is always an issue with me. This was a difficult scene to capture because of the differences in exposure. Looks pretty good...considering.</td>', 'I would have given this a 5. The colors are too oversaturated and the blacks are "clogged". No more laptop for you! :)It''s hard to do a sp. Getting the focus is always an issue with me. This was a difficult scene to capture because of the differences in exposure. Looks pretty good...considering.', '2006-06-12 23:47:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2511525, 343246, 19708, '<td valign="top">But who''s chair is that.... :)<br/>Congrats on the top 20 and your 5th over 6.0 in a row - w00t!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-13 01:24:20.</i></td>', 'But who''s chair is that.... :)Congrats on the top 20 and your 5th over 6.0 in a row - w00t!', '2006-06-13 02:23:28.000000', '2006-06-13 02:24:20.000000', 0),
(2512190, 342726, 36141, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for your effort to comment.<br/> <br/>I know the flair of the window would get me lower points, but as I was DQed just before in another challenge for something I didn''t know I wasn''t allowed to do, I got scared of doing too much to this one, even if it was advanced editing. I''m not to good yet at post processing and didn''t quite know how to get rid of it without making it look worse.<br/> <br/>I took this photo, standing on the attic stairs and there wasn''t any other position to achieve the same atmosphere and the sun was still shining bright.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-13 08:27:19.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all for your effort to comment. I know the flair of the window would get me lower points, but as I was DQed just before in another challenge for something I didn''t know I wasn''t allowed to do, I got scared of doing too much to this one, even if it was advanced editing. I''m not to good yet at post processing and didn''t quite know how to get rid of it without making it look worse. I took this photo, standing on the attic stairs and there wasn''t any other position to achieve the same atmosphere and the sun was still shining bright.', '2006-06-13 09:25:46.000000', '2006-06-13 09:27:19.000000', 0),
